& [Implementation]
  + isolated iterative module exports strict RunPolicy ReadyProjection IterationSuccessor IterationRecord PolicyUsage IterativeRunState StopReason and IterativeReport values
  + default policy is small and every step tool provider and timeout bound is positive and capped
  + ready projection requires the complete validated compact registry and derives only exact handle checkpoint and bounded progress values
  + successor enum makes ready-versus-terminal cardinality exclusive
  + report verifier binds ordered indices predecessor handles exact quota successful compact response successor identity policy usage and compiled nonclaims
  + terminal report projection must equal a fresh derivation from exact observation and the final output must preserve status digest and fixed evidence statement
  + complete report requires terminal evidence reflection identity and no reentry while stopped report requires exact READY head reason and no terminal fields
  + stopped report distinguishes a live reentry handle from a historical handle made unavailable by process restart

& [HonestyAndSecurity]
  + registry validation precedes projection so matching digest labels cannot substitute for admitted content identity
  + READY is explicitly nonterminal and exact state remains under host custody
  + timeout stop cannot precede the declared elapsed boundary
  + restart_unavailable requires false reentry availability and every other stopped reason requires true availability
  + representation and transition consistency do not claim external truth producer authentication or complete causal replay

& [ProofShape]
  + five focused tests cover policy and closed-field rejection report round trip registry-derived projection no state-body leakage stopped and complete exclusivity timeout evidence terminal substitution and predecessor-fork refusal
  + no P0 runtime path main executable provider request or dependency changes

& [Deferred]
  + deterministic stepper provider protocol loopback iterative process replay measurement persistence effects remote access hidden state and FPGA remain unimplemented and unactivated
